---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import VGISubNav from '../../components/sections/VGISubNav.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/ui/PageHead.astro';
import Button from '../../components/ui/Button.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import AgentQuickstart from '../../components/vgi/AgentQuickstart.astro';
import RecordedAgentBuild from '../../components/vgi/RecordedAgentBuild.astro';
import { VGI_AGENT_LANGUAGES, VGI_SKILLS_REPO, vgiSkillsFile } from '../../lib/vgi-agents';
import { organization } from '../../lib/organization';

const description = 'Build and test a VGI worker with Codex, Claude Code, or another coding agent. Choose Python, TypeScript, Go, Rust, Java, or C# and get working SQL, source, and repeatable tests.';
const steps = [
  { number: '01', title: 'Describe the capability', detail: 'A library you want in SQL. An API you want to join. A dataset you want to share.' },
  { number: '02', title: 'Let your agent build it', detail: 'The skill supplies SDK guidance, examples, and the commands to run the worker in your language.' },
  { number: '03', title: 'Finish with a passing query', detail: 'Your agent exercises the worker through a real SQL engine, fixes failures, and leaves repeatable tests.' },
];
const jsonLd = [{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'TechArticle', headline: 'Build a VGI worker with your coding agent', description, url: 'https://query.farm/vgi/build-with-an-agent', author: organization }, { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'VGI', item: 'https://query.farm/vgi/' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Build with an Agent', item: 'https://query.farm/vgi/build-with-an-agent' }] }];
---

<PageLayout title="Build a VGI worker with your coding agent" description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <VGISubNav />
  <PageHead variant="section" eyebrow="VGI for coding agents" title="Your next SQL capability starts with a prompt." hairband>
    <Fragment slot="lede">Choose your language. Describe the function, API, or dataset you want in SQL. Your coding agent builds a VGI worker, runs it, and verifies the result. You get the source and tests to keep extending it.</Fragment>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <Button href="#start" variant="primary" size="md">Build with your agent →</Button>
      <Button href="#recorded-build" variant="secondary" size="md">See a recorded build</Button>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-soil-600">Working SQL in minutes, with the tests to prove it.<br />Codex · Claude Code · Cursor · GitHub Copilot · OpenCode</p>
  </PageHead>

  <section class="section-container py-12 sm:py-16" aria-label="From an idea to tested SQL">
    <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
      {steps.map(step => <div class="border-t border-soil-300 pt-5"><span class="qf-figure text-sm text-sun-700">{step.number}</span><h2 class="mt-3 text-xl text-soil-900">{step.title}</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-700">{step.detail}</p></div>)}
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12"><AgentQuickstart /></div>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 border-b border-soil-300 pb-10 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-700 md:grid-cols-2">
      <p><strong class="text-soil-900">Before you start.</strong> Have your coding agent, your chosen language runtime, and <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/" class="text-link underline underline-offset-2">uv</a> available. The portable installer uses Node.js. The SQL verifier uses stock DuckDB, regardless of the language your worker is written in. Haybarn is also supported.</p>
      <p><strong class="text-soil-900">Start on your machine.</strong> The first worker runs as a local process. You can choose an HTTP service, executable, or another <a href="/vgi/distributing-a-worker" class="text-link underline underline-offset-2">distribution option</a> when you are ready to share it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="what-you-get" class="section-container scroll-mt-32 pb-14 sm:pb-20">
    <div class="grid items-start gap-9 lg:grid-cols-[.9fr_1.1fr]">
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <p class="qf-eyebrow text-sun-700">A project you own</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl text-soil-900">The result is working software.</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-soil-700">A VGI worker is a normal program that exposes typed functions and tables through SQL. The skill helps your agent connect the implementation to the engine and check what comes back.</p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-700">
          <li><strong class="text-soil-900">Source in your language.</strong> Use the libraries and development tools you already know.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-soil-900">Tests you can rerun.</strong> Known values, null behavior, empty input, and multiple batches where they matter.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-soil-900">The exact SQL.</strong> A working launch command, ATTACH statement, and queries against your functions.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-soil-900">A clear handoff.</strong> Dependency versions, verification output, and any remaining failures.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <CodeBlock title="The slugification example · expected SQL behavior" lang="sql" tryable={false} code={`SELECT demo.main.slugify('Hello, VGI!') AS slug;\n-- hello-vgi\n\nSELECT demo.main.slugify('Café crème') AS slug;\n-- cafe-creme\n\nSELECT demo.main.slugify(NULL::VARCHAR) AS slug;\n-- NULL`} />
        <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-soil-300 bg-soil-100 p-5"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-soil-900">Change the idea, keep the workflow.</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-700">Once it works, ask your agent to add an option, expose another function, or wrap your own library. It updates the worker and reruns the tests.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <RecordedAgentBuild />

  <section class="border-y border-soil-300 bg-soil-100 py-12 sm:py-16" id="languages">
    <div class="section-container">
      <p class="qf-eyebrow text-sun-700">Your language, your runtime</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl text-soil-900">Six ways to write the worker.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] leading-relaxed text-soil-700">The skill asks which language you want for a new project and preserves the language of an existing worker. Each recipe points to published SDKs and versioned examples.</p>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-x-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {VGI_AGENT_LANGUAGES.map(language => <a href={`/vgi/docs/${language.id}/`} class="group border-t border-soil-300 py-5 no-underline"><div class="flex items-center justify-between"><h3 class="text-xl text-soil-900">{language.name}</h3><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-link">↗</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-soil-600">{language.runtime}</p><p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-soil-700">{language.sdk}</p></a>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container py-12 sm:py-16" id="verification">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div><p class="qf-eyebrow text-sun-700">Built to be checked</p><h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl text-soil-900">The query is part of the test.</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-soil-700">The skills include a verifier that starts the worker through VGI, executes SQL assertions in DuckDB or Haybarn, and reports the results as JSON. A successful compile is one step; the finished worker must return the expected SQL results.</p><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-soil-700">Add <code>vgi-test</code> to diagnose an existing worker, or <code>vgi-package</code> to produce a local distribution archive with an integrity manifest. <a href={vgiSkillsFile('README.md')} class="text-link underline underline-offset-2">Explore all three skills →</a></p><a href="/vgi/docs/concepts/testing/" class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm text-link underline underline-offset-2">Read the worker testing guide →</a></div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-soil-300 p-6 sm:p-8"><h3 class="text-xl text-soil-900">How close is five minutes?</h3><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-700">A small local function is the right place to start. Completion time depends on the agent, model, language toolchain, dependency downloads, and the capability you ask for.</p><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-700">Our evaluations record elapsed time and human interventions. Treat five minutes as a goal for your first simple worker; an authenticated API or production deployment has more work to do.</p><a href="/blog/build-vgi-workers-with-coding-agents/" class="mt-5 inline-block text-sm font-medium text-link underline underline-offset-2">Read the story behind the skills →</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container pb-16" id="engine">
    <details open class="rounded-xl border border-soil-300 p-5 sm:p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-soil-900">Use stock DuckDB with VGI from Query Farm</summary>
      <div class="mt-4 min-w-0 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-700">
        <p>The quickstart uses stock DuckDB 2.0.0 and the signed VGI build in the <a href="/blog/duckdb-2-query-farm-repository/" class="text-link underline">Query Farm extension repository</a>. The skill handles this setup during verification. To configure your own SQL session:</p>
        <div class="mt-4"><CodeBlock code={`SET allow_extension_repositories = 'allowed';
CREATE EXTENSION REPOSITORY IF NOT EXISTS query_farm
    WITH PREFIX 'https://duckdb-extensions.query.farm';

INSTALL vgi FROM query_farm;
LOAD vgi FROM query_farm;`} lang="sql" tryable={false} /></div>
        <p class="mt-3">In later sessions, use <code>LOAD vgi FROM query_farm</code>. The recorded stock DuckDB checks use macOS ARM64; check the available build for your engine version and platform.</p>
        <p class="mt-3"><a href="/products/haybarn" class="text-link underline">Haybarn</a> is also tested. Existing Haybarn projects can keep their engine and select <code>--engine haybarn</code> in the verifier.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-5"><Button href="#start" variant="primary">Choose your language and start →</Button><a href="/vgi/building-a-worker" class="text-sm text-link underline underline-offset-2">Explore what a worker can expose</a><a href={VGI_SKILLS_REPO} class="text-sm text-link underline underline-offset-2">View the skills on GitHub</a></div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
